{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Grid and Application Architecture for Databases"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These words are used when talking about the grid and application architecture for databases."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to query analysis, and data base engines.  Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level. \tRecognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "resilient "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "flexible "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It produces a resilient and lower cost system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "exceptional "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "outstanding, excellent qualities"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The flexibility grid architecture provides is exceptional! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "silo "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "it refers to databases"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You won't have application silos that may not be used appropriately"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "surpass "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become and do better than others"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This architecture could be surpassed by the multi-tier soon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "optimize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something useful and effective"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The server computers may be optimized to fit the customer needs. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about grid and application architecture. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the different applications, its use and advantages. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short text explaining briefly each one, using modal verbs in passive voice and phrasal verbs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your work with your partners "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive of Modal Verbs "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Modal verbs</strong> are a kind of auxiliary verbs that come with other verbs to express permission, ability or possibility."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are some verbs with their respective denotation:</br> </br> <strong>Can \u2013 May \u2013 Might</strong>:      possibility, ability, permission </br> <strong>Must \u2013 Have to</strong>:             obligation </br> <strong>Should</strong>:                   \t  suggestion</br></br>  Example:</br><span class=\"italic\"> Michael <strong>can swim</strong> fast.</span> </br> <span class=\"italic\">The athlete <strong>must keep</strong> an appropriate diet.</span> </br></br>  Notice that these verbs do not take \u2013es/-s at the end of the verb in the third person singular. For questions, they come at the beginning: </br></br> Example:</br> <span class=\"italic\"><strong>Can</strong> you<strong> ride </strong>a bike? </span></br> <span class=\"italic\"><strong>Should</strong> I <strong>tell</strong> mom about it? </span></br></br>  We used <strong>modal verbs</strong> in their <strong>passive form</strong> when the important element is the object of the action, and not the person who performs it. </br></br>  We follow this structure: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + Modal verb + be + Past participle verb + complement</div></br></br>  Example:</br> <span class=\"italic\">Many applications <strong>can be used</strong> to increase the flexibility in our database.</div>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It may be surpassed by the multi-tier soon. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This can be seen as one of its main advantages."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Phrasal verbs</strong> are verbs composed of two words, a verb and a preposition,  that have a different meaning from the original verb. A group of them is separable, while others are inseparable."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Phrasal verbs </strong>are made up of two or more words. For example: </br></br>  <strong>Make</strong>: create</br> <strong>Up</strong>: that points towards or higher</br> <strong>Make + up</strong>: to compensate. </br></br>Separable phrasal verbs are those verbs whose direct object can be inserted between the verb and the preposition. See this example:</br></br><span class=\"italic\">Option 1. I have to <span class=\"strong\">give back</span> the book to the library.</span></br><span class=\"italic\">Option 2. I have to <span class=\"strong\">give</span> the book <span class=\"strong\">back</span> to the library.</span></br></br>  There are some <strong>phrasal verbs</strong> called \u201cinseparable\u201d because the words can never be set apart. </br></br>  Examples: </br>    <span class=\"italic\"> I need to <strong>come out with</strong> a new idea.</span> <strong> (correct) </strong> </br><span class=\"italic\">I need to <strong>come out</strong> a new idea <strong>with</strong>.</span> <strong> (incorrect) </strong> </br> <span class=\"italic\"> I need to <strong>come</strong> a new idea <strong>out with</strong>. </span><span class=\"strong\">(incorrect)</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Meaning</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"come out with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">produce, utter</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go on with \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">continue</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go over\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">review</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"settle on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">decide</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"count on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">rely</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"get away with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">do something without being caught</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pass on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">transmit</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"keep up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">working to be at the same level than someone</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sure! But try to keep up with me, okay?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let me go over the client/server architecture. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for more information about grid and application architecture. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe the different applications, its utilities and advantages."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a short text explaining briefly each one, using the grammar and vocabulary studied."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss your work with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Mary</span>: I want to know more about Grid and Application architecture, can you help me?\n<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Billy</span>: Sure! But try to keep up with me, okay? Grid architecture is simple and it can be used by any company. It produces a resilient and lower cost system; this can be seen as one of its main advantages.\n<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Mary</span>: Is it true that independent, modular hardware and software can be connected depending on the needs of the customer with grid computing?"}, {"time": "30500", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Billy</span>: Yes! The flexibility grid architecture provides is exceptional! Besides, different problems may be solved thanks to it. For example, you won't have application silos that may not be used appropriately, or systems that become difficult to change and expensive to maintain.\n<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Mary</span>: I see. And, what can be said about Application Architecture? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Billy</span>: Well, there are two common database architectures, client/server and multitier. Let me go over the client/server architecture. It's simple; on the one hand, we have a client, which is a database application that requests and processes data; they use different computers from the servers. On the other hand, we have the servers. Servers receive and process the requests that are generated by the client applications. Data must always be managed and kept by a server; the server computers may be optimized to fit the customer needs. This architecture could be surpassed by the multi-tier soon."}, {"time": "106500", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Mary</span>: What is multitier, though? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Billy</span>: The multi-tier has the same elements: a client and a database server, but they use one or more application servers as a bridge between the client and the database server. The application servers provide access and remove load work from the end server. The application server is a tool that validates users' credentials, allows a fast connection to the database servers, and even performs the operations requested by the client."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le03ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le03ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "templa